## How each report is placed

1. Count each report id once. The export pages overlap, so some reports come twice.
2. A report the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) is a one-day move. Its body shows a
   date one day off, or two attendees on two different days. It is not a swap.
3. Every other report goes by its tenant, as `causes.ts` reads it: a day-first tenant on the
   booking-v3 form is `hint`, and the rest are `parser`.

The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It does not decide the problem.

## Lessons

- Read what the reports show before you merge them. A swap and a one-day move are two bugs.
- One fix per ticket. If a fix cannot close every report in a ticket, split the ticket.

